<p>A coalition of International Energy Agency (IEA) member countries agreed to release a record 400 million barrels of oil from emergency reserves, aiming to cool a sharp rise in crude prices tied to supply disruptions during the war involving Iran. The goal is to get more oil into the system quickly and help steady energy markets. In the U.S., President Trump authorized a release of 172 million barrels from the Strategic Petroleum Reserve. Deliveries are expected to begin next week as part of the coordinated IEA effort.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/6KEXrZ_TfxoInLv8web5Qj93M8tGjy_tCxz1j-SupfnKvhtYodRwSFfbW5lgQEETKR1g43T5JR66l_QjEPxRAlwl4qRHu-_C2qnSzek0a6Jof7Vi3lo07-a0dkoUr2J4dfAk-UMKBXoLXBJ7YUGp1qOfhFr0j3u8IGWbpbHQ0NhvOd1lVYtMTgmdeO_O19R6vAaSlEYHSk8_UDVzB1O_plZYStScpg' alt='People filling up at a gas station in Los Angeles on Wednesday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Scope and vote: The IEA said member countries agreed unanimously, calling it the biggest coordinated drawdown of emergency stocks in its history; some coverage also pointed to the wider agreement among the agency’s 32 member nations.</li><li>How the IEA framed it: PBS reported the Paris-based agency said it would “make” oil available from members’ emergency reserves as wealthy nations try to steady energy markets.</li><li>Immediate market test: Semafor and AllSides reported oil prices didn’t fall after the announcement, a sign traders were still focused on the war-driven risk of further supply disruptions.</li><li>Why it may not be enough: Al Jazeera argued a one-off reserve release can be swamped by expectations of a longer disruption; analysts quoted by CBS said any relief is likely to be short-lived and depends on how long the conflict-related supply hit lasts.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>International Energy Agency (IEA): The IEA said member countries unanimously backed its biggest-ever coordinated release of emergency reserves to respond to soaring prices linked to the war involving Iran. (<a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-03-11-0700/energy-dozens-countries-agreed-release-400-million-barrels-oil-it-didnt-bring-down-prices'>AllSides</a>)</li><li>U.S. government: The U.S. Department of Energy said the Strategic Petroleum Reserve release will start next week, meant to ease gasoline prices as the Middle East war ripples through oil markets. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/us-to-release-172-million-barrels-from-strategic-oil-reserve-to-cut-prices-11203057#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li><li>Market analysts (as cited): Analysts quoted by CBS said the emergency release could bring some near-term relief, but the bigger question is how long conflict-driven supply fears continue to dominate the market. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/international-energy-agency-release-oil-amid-iran-war/'>CBS News</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2026/3/12/why-historic-oil-reserves-release-may-do-little-to-bring-down-rising-prices'>Why historic release of oil reserves may not tame surging prices</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-03-11-0700/energy-dozens-countries-agreed-release-400-million-barrels-oil-it-didnt-bring-down-prices'>Dozens of countries agreed to release 400 million barrels of oil. But it didn&#x27;t bring down prices.</a> - allsides.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/iea-to-release-400-million-barrels-of-oil-as-iran-war-disrupts-global-supply-ws-e-13988520.html'>IEA to release 400 million barrels of oil as Iran war disrupts global supply</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/economy/iea-agrees-to-release-record-volume-of-emergency-oil-reserves-in-effort-to-calm-prices'>Wealthy nations pledge a record release of emergency oil reserves in bid to calm surging prices</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/international-energy-agency-release-oil-amid-iran-war/'>IEA to re